:answer/id #uuid "b670f12b-6ddf-5c4d-b961-d054354c05e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "270" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279688} :answer-field/id #uuid "10ffcf17-651b-596d-9841-08ccdfc42bc7" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279687}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bdb7a25f-1f4a-5b5e-9bf8-a8766f4279fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-328351" :question/problem "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, the **exact solutions** to the equation $4\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘})+4=0,$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{3}=$\n{{field-3}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{4}=$\n{{field-4}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘})+4 & =0 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘}) & =-4 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘}) & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-{45}^{∘} & =-{45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={45}^{∘}-{45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 2x & =n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & =n\\cdot {90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={0}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={90}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x={180}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x={270}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ \n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={0}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}={90}^{∘},\\,{x}_{3}={180}^{∘},\\,{x}_{4}={270}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279689 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3bd5e5c-b8d1-53e5-9968-8bef8faceb4b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing the Tangent Function Transformed by Multiple Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07eb5011-0b61-5397-8672-df521058b667" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279691} {:answer/id #uuid "b110e858-fe2e-5b2b-ab5c-9cf4b7bcf38b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279692}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07eb5011-0b61-5397-8672-df521058b667" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279691} :answer-field/id #uuid "c48efbfe-5dfd-533b-9edb-c8e1a25b7997" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279690} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72027805-7d5a-51e4-b77a-0dc7b6694270" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72027805-7d5a-51e4-b77a-0dc7b6694270" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279694} :answer-field/id #uuid "507681ac-c656-5071-b7dd-e1503f6dc8b5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279693} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "174fe84e-9618-5ac1-b9b7-3c467ea339a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "174fe84e-9618-5ac1-b9b7-3c467ea339a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279696} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c0d0826-75a3-5298-a5be-331431fe1a97" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279695} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd75b594-a102-5dbf-8ae2-ace83fd5e293" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd75b594-a102-5dbf-8ae2-ace83fd5e293" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279698} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ba43f6d-0b94-5ec9-ae16-6046265db6fb" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ddd02a1-a73a-57ac-a8bf-4cce5189dc0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ddd02a1-a73a-57ac-a8bf-4cce5189dc0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279700} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c4f7293-dfdb-5d8d-9c60-8c2072630724" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279699} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "779b37d5-ebf3-5065-b518-9282d7302fea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279702}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "779b37d5-ebf3-5065-b518-9282d7302fea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279702} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9aac4cb-4f02-5950-b098-4a47f2cb7be0" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279701} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6fe8c16-f73f-5f89-ae14-76bc898878f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6fe8c16-f73f-5f89-ae14-76bc898878f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279704} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e680df8-6a0a-5a87-b627-1237c7363719" :answer-field/key "field-7" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279703} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4820e11e-46e2-52b3-9ab6-9f53ea6c8b4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4820e11e-46e2-52b3-9ab6-9f53ea6c8b4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279706} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffb4073c-e853-56f7-8a64-854a42c4fdc7" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279705}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "05d62ebd-da1d-59cf-9c43-a246ead9b2bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-328359" :question/problem "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, the **exact solutions** to the equation  $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\sqrt{3},$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$  are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,{x}_{3}=$\n{{field-3}}$,\\,{x}_{4}=$\n{{field-4}}\n\n${x}_{5}=$\n{{field-5}}$,\\,{x}_{6}=$\n{{field-6}}$,\\,{x}_{7}=$\n{{field-7}}$,\\,{x}_{8}=$\n{{field-8}}." :question/worked-solution "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-\\frac{\\pi }{3} & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi  \\\\ 4x & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(3n+2)\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=4$ gives $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}$\n\n- Setting $n=5$ gives $x=\\frac{17\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=6$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$\n\n- Setting $n=7$ gives $x=\\frac{23\\pi }{12}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ \n\nSo, the solutions to the equation, in ascending order, are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\,{x}_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{12},\\,{x}_{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3},\\,{x}_{4}=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}, \\\\ {x}_{5} & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6},\\,{x}_{6}=\\frac{17\\pi }{12},\\,{x}_{7}=\\frac{5\\pi }{3},\\,{x}_{8}=\\frac{23\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279707 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9eb12a99-5169-52f7-8830-5de0d2d854f6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing a Transformed Tangent Function Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8149a868-11b5-5f9d-8fb1-39dfb7d01979" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8149a868-11b5-5f9d-8fb1-39dfb7d01979" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279709} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7c88d87-d7a4-5364-aea1-b16bcbed6338" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279708} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3be3081-5f86-5ead-9f37-e3d507d656a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3be3081-5f86-5ead-9f37-e3d507d656a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279711} :answer-field/id #uuid "c505558b-5e80-54a1-8424-cc1bcb958ec4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279710} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e29cd1c-b788-57d8-a024-17a1c0d26b9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e29cd1c-b788-57d8-a024-17a1c0d26b9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279713} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d742008-a4ee-58cd-83b6-bbb26e431c1d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279712} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f7e081a-ddcc-541d-8ec8-0c286f0c65f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f7e081a-ddcc-541d-8ec8-0c286f0c65f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279715} :answer-field/id #uuid "a395fad7-0f4e-5aa4-9141-385c9258da87" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279714}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cbb01e88-b572-58bc-9bf4-e3da4c96ce22" :question/math-academy-id "q-328366" :question/problem "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, the **exact solutions** to the equation  $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)=-1,$ for $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi ,$  are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,{x}_{3}=$\n{{field-3}}$,\\,{x}_{4}=$\n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(4n-1)\\pi }{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=-\\frac{5\\pi }{8}$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{8}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{8}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{8}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi .$ \n\nSo, in ascending order,  the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-\\frac{5\\pi }{8},\\,{x}_{2}=-\\frac{\\pi }{8},\\,{x}_{3}=\\frac{3\\pi }{8},\\,{x}_{4}=\\frac{7\\pi }{8}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9eb12a99-5169-52f7-8830-5de0d2d854f6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing a Transformed Tangent Function Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0355ca6-5828-5463-8acc-5160551e38d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279718} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e66774-751c-5eea-8d10-4af132761eff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279719} {:answer/id #uuid "3e5ce4eb-db38-527d-85ab-c79beedfc8ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{\\pi }^{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279720} {:answer/id #uuid "776d8315-d5bd-551b-987e-b69082eacc0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279721} {:answer/id #uuid "f2983b5d-1f05-5e94-a60e-527bcb6f953e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "776d8315-d5bd-551b-987e-b69082eacc0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279721} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec58a1e8-7a8c-578f-97cd-11bdb61534c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279717}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "32385bf9-21f8-5ffa-a56e-a6ed215bd301" :question/math-academy-id "q-65855" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the exact solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡2x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ for $0\\le x<\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(6n-1)\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$ So, the solutions are $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{12},\\frac{11\\pi }{12}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{12}+\\frac{11\\pi }{12}=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f40f50e-49a7-5eda-b642-dc7085569b23" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing the Tangent Function Transformed by One Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "903c775c-a4de-51e6-9023-4b0a2bea481b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279725} {:answer/id #uuid "566d92f6-8349-56d3-9c02-044fc04c0520" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279726} {:answer/id #uuid "eb63d6ea-4243-5a06-b480-4a21ee7bd9be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279727} {:answer/id #uuid "310b6767-26d7-534d-a546-f835f25e0de4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279728} {:answer/id #uuid "c0b88ef1-ee30-5601-9b00-b47526b8a1a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\,125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "310b6767-26d7-534d-a546-f835f25e0de4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279728} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf69e643-65fe-5802-bf2a-78b9ed931736" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279724}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6afa4a52-7356-528a-a2ed-e03d8f3d6887" :question/math-academy-id "q-82372" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the exact solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-{90}^{∘})=-1$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-{90}^{∘} & =-{45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={90}^{∘}-{45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={45}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={225}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ So, the solutions are $x={45}^{∘},{225}^{∘}.$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is $45\\cdot 225=10\\,125.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3bd5e5c-b8d1-53e5-9968-8bef8faceb4b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing the Tangent Function Transformed by Multiple Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b553140f-b61c-5f39-88cb-4e344b4772b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "π^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091230} {:answer/id #uuid "be56e4de-5122-5ddb-9bd0-49f9962cc8b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3π^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091231} {:answer/id #uuid "127414c5-ffff-53bf-b4cb-d44417352fd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3π^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091232} {:answer/id #uuid "558e68bd-93e3-5749-98f7-519245e1f96a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091233} {:answer/id #uuid "656fd5c1-d10b-50e7-b6ad-722f2a2d1221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "656fd5c1-d10b-50e7-b6ad-722f2a2d1221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091234} :answer-field/id #uuid "682d2993-e4a0-586b-8bc0-2358e2bbe137" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091229}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d843ce6f-ede9-5fe9-8998-219097a4dac3" :question/math-academy-id "q-8482" :question/problem "Consider the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-\\sqrt{3}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ Given that the exact solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are written in ascending order, what is the value of ${x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}?$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{\\pi }{3} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=0$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\pi $\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx=0,\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and ${x}_{3}=\\pi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot \\pi =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092807 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9eb12a99-5169-52f7-8830-5de0d2d854f6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing a Transformed Tangent Function Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d886652-ac3c-5913-9fd2-d4d1d592b29d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091308} {:answer/id #uuid "e68dbdd8-430a-54f7-bdcc-c28d7323c563" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5π}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091309} {:answer/id #uuid "f808a855-0eb4-56aa-a3aa-f2442ed6d842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091310} {:answer/id #uuid "0a337708-3a18-578f-b28b-c4b4ccdd7732" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091311} {:answer/id #uuid "2e51bf90-cce6-5a94-88af-d9d2b2d52ff1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f808a855-0eb4-56aa-a3aa-f2442ed6d842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091310} :answer-field/id #uuid "e247bfa5-3146-5d6d-af6e-c3231dc42840" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "031552db-aefc-5369-b9be-0f86727e7b83" :question/math-academy-id "q-8550" :question/problem "Consider the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi .$ If the exact solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are written in ascending order, what is the value of ${x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+\\frac{\\pi }{3} & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(6n-1)\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=-\\frac{7\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi .$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{7\\pi }{12},\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{12},\\,\\frac{5\\pi }{12},\\,\\frac{11\\pi }{12}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ and ${x}_{3}=\\frac{5\\pi }{12},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{5\\pi }{12}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092808 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9eb12a99-5169-52f7-8830-5de0d2d854f6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing a Transformed Tangent Function Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "932c9431-c4b6-50ca-bd9a-fb05eba62cdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091314} {:answer/id #uuid "bddf8b6b-6d8e-5c1a-912b-cb1089db461d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091315} {:answer/id #uuid "dac02fa8-4304-5b0d-a0e1-fa5714b12af1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3π}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091316} {:answer/id #uuid "dfb6326b-009a-57c6-ae9d-62f33d37abde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091317} {:answer/id #uuid "02eb1083-6d2b-50c0-879c-9673f0e0c266" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "932c9431-c4b6-50ca-bd9a-fb05eba62cdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091314} :answer-field/id #uuid "d654b2ab-496c-5a14-94ce-a4465b3f660a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091313}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "81cddf32-b2f0-5da6-954a-aa9d5faf5fcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-8556" :question/problem "Consider the equation $\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})+3=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi .$ If the exact solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are written in ascending order, what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{4}?$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})+3 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =-3 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi .$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ and ${x}_{4}=\\frac{3\\pi }{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{4}=-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+\\frac{3\\pi }{4}=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279730 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3bd5e5c-b8d1-53e5-9968-8bef8faceb4b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing the Tangent Function Transformed by Multiple Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00ccd903-5c24-528a-8d48-63546a00977a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279732} {:answer/id #uuid "1fd32d65-a4a8-5abf-af77-2ed08981df9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279733} {:answer/id #uuid "f55bf7fb-6cdd-5bb7-8d02-fa0a1b30f7b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279734} {:answer/id #uuid "ab28603e-6e91-573d-a88c-c9e594b82560" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279735} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d74da3-5418-53e7-a8a4-5d086c60c804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fd32d65-a4a8-5abf-af77-2ed08981df9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279733} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8d04fa4-e2a1-588e-a8ca-2887dac48ff9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b2133d03-8737-5ad8-a61a-2ae63b6db3e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-8558" :question/problem "Consider the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{7\\pi }{3})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ If the exact solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are written in ascending order, what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{4}?$" :question/worked-solution "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+\\frac{7\\pi }{3} & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =-\\frac{7\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =-\\frac{13\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{13\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(6n-13)\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=4$ gives $x=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=5$ gives $x=\\frac{17\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=6$ gives $x=\\frac{23\\pi }{12}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5\\pi }{12},\\,\\frac{11\\pi }{12},\\,\\frac{17\\pi }{12},\\,\\frac{23\\pi }{12}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${x}_{1}=\\frac{5\\pi }{12}$ and ${x}_{4}=\\frac{23\\pi }{12},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{4}=\\frac{5\\pi }{12}+\\frac{23\\pi }{12}=\\frac{28\\pi }{12}=\\frac{7\\pi }{3}.\n$$"}]}
